{"id":"mahabharata-12-281","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":281,"title":"एकाशीत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 281 · Who helps whom","summary":{"en":"Parashara says that each creature acts for itself and tells how kings such as Shaibya won a high place by giving, as by feeding the sage Mathara with fruits and leaves. He lists the great sages who rose by austerity and says that the learned man who, giving up pride, serves the old is honoured by the good.","kn":"ಪ್ರತಿ ಜೀವಿಯೂ ತನಗಾಗಿ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂದು ಪರಾಶರ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶೈಬ್ಯ ಮುಂತಾದ ರಾಜರು ದಾನದಿಂದ ಉನ್ನತ ಸ್ಥಾನ ಪಡೆದ ಕಥೆ, ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಉನ್ನತರಾದ ಮಹರ್ಷಿಗಳ ಪಟ್ಟಿ. ಅಹಂಕಾರ ತೊರೆದು ವೃದ್ಧರನ್ನು ಸೇವಿಸುವ ವಿದ್ವಾಂಸ ಸಜ್ಜನರಿಂದ ಗೌರವಿಸಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पराशर कहते हैं कि हर प्राणी अपने ही लिए कर्म करता है, और बताते हैं कि शैब्य जैसे राजाओं ने दान से उच्च स्थान पाया। वे तप से ऊँचे उठे महर्षियों के नाम गिनाते हैं और कहते हैं कि अभिमान छोड़कर वृद्धों की सेवा करने वाला विद्वान सज्जनों से सम्मानित होता है।","te":"ప్రతి జీవి తన కోసమే పనిచేస్తుందని పరాశరుడు చెబుతాడు; శైబ్యుడు వంటి రాజులు దానంతో ఉన్నత స్థానం పొందిన కథ, తపస్సుతో ఎదిగిన మహర్షుల పట్టిక ఇస్తాడు. అహంకారం విడిచి పెద్దలను సేవించే పండితుడు సజ్జనులచే గౌరవింపబడతాడు.","ta":"ஒவ்வொரு உயிரும் தனக்காகவே செயல்படுகிறது என்று பராசரர் கூறி, சைப்யன் போன்ற மன்னர்கள் தானத்தால் உயர்ந்த இடம் பெற்றதையும் தவத்தால் உயர்ந்த மகரிஷிகளையும் பட்டியலிடுகிறார். செருக்கை விட்டு முதியோருக்குப் பணிவிடை செய்யும் அறிஞர் நல்லோரால் மதிக்கப்படுகிறார்.","ml":"ഓരോ ജീവിയും സ്വയം പ്രവർത്തിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് പരാശരൻ പറയുന്നു; ശൈബ്യൻ പോലുള്ള രാജാക്കന്മാർ മാഥരമുനിക്ക് പഴങ്ങളും ഇലകളും നൽകിയതുപോലുള്ള ദാനത്താൽ ഉന്നത സ്ഥാനം നേടിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. തപസ്സാൽ ഉയർന്ന മഹാമുനിമാരുടെ പട്ടിക അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു; അഹങ്കാരം ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച് വൃദ്ധരെ സേവിക്കുന്ന പണ്ഡിതൻ നല്ലവരാൽ ആദരിക്കപ്പെടുന്നുവെന്ന് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.281; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"पराशर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Parashara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कः कस्य चोपकुरुते कश्च कस्मै प्रयच्छति ।\nप्राणी करोत्ययं कर्म सर्वमात्मार्थमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who helps whom, and who gives to whom? A living being does all his actions himself, for his own sake."}},{"n":2,"text":"गौरवेण परित्यक्तं निःस्नेहं परिवर्जयेत् ।\nसोदर्यं भ्रातरमपि किमुतान्यं पृथग्जनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should avoid a person who has abandoned one out of pride and has no affection, even a brother from the same womb, and much more an ordinary stranger."}},{"n":3,"text":"विशिष्टस्य विशिष्टाच्च तुल्यौ दानप्रतिग्रहौ ।\nतयोः पुण्यतरं दानं तद्द्विजस्य प्रयच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving and receiving between a distinguished giver and a distinguished receiver are equal; but of the two, the gift is the more meritorious one made to a Brahmin."}},{"n":4,"text":"न्यायागतं धनं वर्णैर्न्यायेनैव विवर्धितम् ।\nसंरक्ष्यं यत्नमास्थाय धर्मार्थमिति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth that has come by right means and been increased by right means, among all the classes, should be guarded with effort for the sake of dharma; so it is settled."}},{"n":5,"text":"न धर्मार्थी नृशंसेन कर्मणा धनमर्जयेत् ।\nशक्तितः सर्वकार्याणि कुर्यान्नर्द्धिमनुस्मरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who seeks dharma should not earn wealth by cruel action. He should do all tasks according to his strength and should not keep thinking of prosperity."}},{"n":6,"text":"अपो हि प्रयतः शीतास्तापिता ज्वलनेन वा ।\nशक्तितोऽतिथये दत्त्वा क्षुधार्तायाश्नुते फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even pure water, cold or heated by fire, given according to one's ability to a guest tormented by hunger, earns the fruit."}},{"n":7,"text":"रन्तिदेवेन लोकेष्टा सिद्धिः प्राप्ता महात्मना ।\nफलपत्रैरथो मूलैर्मुनीनर्चितवानसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Rantideva attained the perfection that people long for; he honored sages with fruits, leaves and roots."}},{"n":8,"text":"तैरेव फलपत्रैश्च स माठरमतोषयत् ।\nतस्माल्लेभे परं स्थानं शैब्योऽपि पृथिवीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With those same fruits and leaves he pleased Mathara; and from this the king of the Shibis too gained a supreme state."}},{"n":9,"text":"देवतातिथिभृत्येभ्यः पितृभ्योऽथात्मनस्तथा ।\nऋणवाञ्जायते मर्त्यस्तस्मादनृणतां व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A mortal is born in debt to the gods, to guests, to dependents, to the ancestors and to himself; so he should become free of debt."}},{"n":10,"text":"स्वाध्यायेन महर्षिभ्यो देवेभ्यो यज्ञकर्मणा ।\nपितृभ्यः श्राद्धदानेन नृणामभ्यर्चनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does so by study to the great sages, by sacrifice to the gods, by the offering of shraddha to the ancestors, and by honoring men."}},{"n":11,"text":"वाचः शेषावहार्येण पालनेनात्मनोऽपि च ।\nयथावद्भृत्यवर्गस्य चिकीर्षेद्धर्ममादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should wish to practice dharma from the start by keeping the remainder of one's speech under control, by protecting oneself, and by properly caring for the group of dependents."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रयत्नेन च संसिद्धा धनैरपि विवर्जिताः ।\nसम्यग्घुत्वा हुतवहं मुनयः सिद्धिमागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even without wealth, sages who strove hard and offered rightly into the fire reached perfection."}},{"n":13,"text":"विश्वामित्रस्य पुत्रत्वमृचीकतनयोऽगमत् ।\nऋग्भिः स्तुत्वा महाभागो देवान्वै यज्ञभागिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Richika became the son of Vishvamitra, having praised with Rig verses the gods who share in sacrifice and being greatly fortunate."}},{"n":14,"text":"गतः शुक्रत्वमुशना देवदेवप्रसादनात् ।\nदेवीं स्तुत्वा तु गगने मोदते तेजसा वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ushanas gained the state of Shukra by pleasing the god of gods; and having praised the goddess he rejoices in the sky, surrounded by radiance."}},{"n":15,"text":"असितो देवलश्चैव तथा नारदपर्वतौ ।\nकक्षीवाञ्जामदग्न्यश्च रामस्ताण्ड्यस्तथांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asita and Devala, Narada and Parvata, Kakshivan, the son of Jamadagni, Rama, Tandya and Amshuman,"}},{"n":16,"text":"वसिष्ठो जमदग्निश्च विश्वामित्रोऽत्रिरेव च ।\nभरद्वाजो हरिश्मश्रुः कुण्डधारः श्रुतश्रवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha, Jamadagni, Vishvamitra and Atri, Bharadvaja, Harishmashru, Kundadhara and Shrutashravas:"}},{"n":17,"text":"एते महर्षयः स्तुत्वा विष्णुमृग्भिः समाहिताः ।\nलेभिरे तपसा सिद्धिं प्रसादात्तस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"these great sages, having praised Vishnu with Rig verses, collected in mind, gained perfection through austerity by the grace of that wise one."}},{"n":18,"text":"अनर्हाश्चार्हतां प्राप्ताः सन्तः स्तुत्वा तमेव ह ।\nन तु वृद्धिमिहान्विच्छेत्कर्म कृत्वा जुगुप्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some who were unworthy attained worthiness by praising him alone; but one should not seek prosperity here by doing despised action."}},{"n":19,"text":"येऽर्था धर्मेण ते सत्या येऽधर्मेण धिगस्तु तान् ।\nधर्मं वै शाश्वतं लोके न जह्याद्धनकाङ्क्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth gained by dharma is true wealth; as for that gained by adharma, shame on it. One should not abandon the eternal dharma in the world out of desire for wealth."}},{"n":20,"text":"आहिताग्निर्हि धर्मात्मा यः स पुण्यकृदुत्तमः ।\nवेदा हि सर्वे राजेन्द्र स्थितास्त्रिष्वग्निषु प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the man of dharma who keeps the sacred fires is the best of the merit-doers; and all the Vedas, king of kings, rest in the three fires."}},{"n":21,"text":"स चाप्यग्न्याहितो विप्रः क्रिया यस्य न हीयते ।\nश्रेयो ह्यनाहिताग्नित्वमग्निहोत्रं न निष्क्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That Brahmin too, whose rites do not lapse, is a keeper of the fires; better to keep no fire than an Agnihotra with no action."}},{"n":22,"text":"अग्निरात्मा च माता च पिता जनयिता तथा ।\nगुरुश्च नरशार्दूल परिचर्या यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire, the self, mother, father, the begetter and the teacher: service to these, tiger among men, is to be done as is right."}},{"n":23,"text":"मानं त्यक्त्वा यो नरो वृद्धसेवी\nविद्वान्क्लीबः पश्यति प्रीतियोगात् ।\nदाक्ष्येणाहीनो धर्मयुक्तो नदान्तो\nलोकेऽस्मिन्वै पूज्यते सद्भिरार्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man who, giving up pride, serves the elders, the learned even if gentle and unmanly, who sees things through affection and is not lacking in skill, who is joined to dharma and self-controlled, is honored in this world by the good as a noble one."}}]}]}